## Implementation (core logic)
```tcl
proc pattern_speed_weekly_stats {manifest} {
    set total 0; set valid 0
    set n_no_folder 0; set n_only_irunlog 0; set n_empty 0; set n_no_speed 0
    set lo ""; set hi ""

    foreach rec $manifest {
        incr total
        set name [lindex $rec 0]; set fe [lindex $rec 1]
        set ff   [lindex $rec 2]; set mt [lindex $rec 3]

        set root [regsub {\.avc$} $name {}]
        set fields [split $root "_"]
        if {[llength $fields] < 2} { incr n_no_speed; continue }
        set speed [lindex $fields end-1]   ;# SECOND-TO-LAST field

        if {!$fe}                          { incr n_no_folder;  continue }
        if {[llength $ff] == 0}            { incr n_empty;       continue }
        if {[llength $ff] == 1 && [string equal [lindex $ff 0] "irun.log"]} {
            incr n_only_irunlog; continue
        }

        incr valid
        if {[info exists speed_count($speed)]} { incr speed_count($speed) } else { set speed_count($speed) 1 }
        set wk [clock format $mt -format %G-W%V -gmt 1]
        if {[info exists week_count($wk)]} { incr week_count($wk) } else { set week_count($wk) 1 }
        set wsk "$wk:$speed"
        if {[info exists week_speed($wsk)]} { incr week_speed($wsk) } else { set week_speed($wsk) 1 }
        if {$lo eq "" || $mt < $lo} { set lo $mt }
        if {$hi eq "" || $mt > $hi} { set hi $mt }
    }

    set speeds [lsort -integer -unique [array names speed_count]]
    set speed_totals {}; foreach sp $speeds { lappend speed_totals "$sp:$speed_count($sp)" }
    set weeks [lsort [array names week_count]]
    set week_totals {};  foreach wk $weeks  { lappend week_totals "$wk:$week_count($wk)" }
    set week_speed_items {}
    foreach wk $weeks {
        foreach sp $speeds {
            set wsk "$wk:$sp"
            if {[info exists week_speed($wsk)]} { lappend week_speed_items "$wsk:$week_speed($wsk)" }
        }
    }

    return [join [list total_avc $total total_valid $valid \
                num_no_folder $n_no_folder num_only_irunlog $n_only_irunlog \
                num_empty $n_empty num_no_speed $n_no_speed \
                time_span_lo $lo time_span_hi $hi \
                speeds [join $speeds " "] speed_totals [join $speed_totals " "] \
                weeks [join $weeks " "] week_totals [join $week_totals " "] \
                week_speed [join $week_speed_items " "]] " "]
}
```

Key design choices:
- Speed is `[lindex $fields end-1]` (second-to-last `_` field), avoiding the last-field traps (001/996/007).
- Strict folder validation order: missing folder → empty → only `irun.log`.
- Uses associative arrays (portable across Tcl 8.x) instead of `dict`; `%G-W%V` with `-gmt 1` for ISO-week labels.
- Numeric speed sort via `lsort -integer`; weeks via plain lexicographic sort (valid since `%V` is zero-padded); `week_speed` ordered by week then (numeric) speed.
- Flat single-line output, list-valued keys placed last so each list is terminated by the next key.

